	(text "Task 13 audit fix (F3, minor): D30/R121 -- spec S10 PD-good indicator, missing since Task 4 dropped the LED. +3V3->R121(1k)->D30->CH224K_PG (kill gate removed 2026-07-19; was LED_PWR). CH224K_PG is open-drain, active-low (WCH CH224K datasheet: pulls to GND once PD negotiation succeeds; datasheet explicitly lists driving an indicator LED as a typical use). Checked R4 (10k pull-up, CH224K_PG to +3V3, from Task 4): it does NOT conflict with D30 -- it defines a clean idle-high (LED off) state when PG is unasserted and adds only ~0.33mA of extra sink current when PG pulls low (LED on); R4 is kept as-is, not replaced."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2dbbc2c9-b07b-4394-bc61-9338411c0407")
	)
	(text "Task 13 audit fix (F3, minor): D29/R120 -- spec S10 12V-node/power indicator, missing since Task 4 dropped the LED (drift, never amended). +3V3->R120(1k)->D29->GND (kill gate removed 2026-07-19; was LED_PWR). +3V3 is only alive once the +12V node has been negotiated -- per the F1 fix pass (R40/R41 BUCK_EN divider corrected), the buck reliably starts ~8V+, never at 5V pre-negotiation. So D29 correctly indicates negotiated-12V-present, not raw VBUS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 554.99 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84423a43-f8be-4b72-aca3-f902777a8f06")
	)
	(text "TODO(mcu): POE_STATUS net dropped on this sheet — EVM-093 exposes BT only as an isolated LED indicator (U23 opto, D16/R38 from +12V_POE). Node N_BTSTAT swings ~0-11V, NOT 3V3-safe. Re-plan the MCU status input (e.g. repurpose U23 collector with a +3V3 pull-up in place of the D16/R38 LED chain) before wiring the mcu sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 539.75 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "879a555d-fbc6-4c39-b1f5-9b569b700138")
	)
